.TH PRINTENV 1 "September 2026" "mitos-utils 0.1.0" "MITOS User Commands"
.SH NAME
printenv \- print environment variables
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B printenv
[\fINAME\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Print the value of each named environment variable, or every variable if none are named.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
Every mitos-utils command additionally accepts \fB\-\-help\fR (print a usage line and exit) and \fB\-\-version\fR. Commands that take file/path arguments also accept \fB\-\-\fR to mark the end of options, so a file literally named e.g. \fB\-oddfile\fR can still be referenced.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 if every named variable was found, 1 if any was unset.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mitos\-box (1),
.BR mitos\-utils\-compat (7),
.BR mitos\-utils\-integration (7)
